{
  "title": "Calm Stretch Census",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA weather station lists daily temperatures. A stretch of consecutive days is calm when its hottest day and coldest day differ by at most `limit` degrees. Count how many non-empty stretches are calm; stretches at different positions count separately even if their values match.\n\n## Input\n\n- `temps` — a list of integers. It may be empty.\n- `limit` — a non-negative integer.\n\n## Output\n\nAn integer: the number of calm stretches.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\ncalm_stretch_census([1, 3, 2], 1)  # returns 4\ncalm_stretch_census([4, 4, 4], 0)  # returns 6\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of `temps` ≤ 10^5\n- -10^9 ≤ each temperature ≤ 10^9\n- 0 ≤ `limit` ≤ 2 * 10^9\n- The answer can reach about 5 billion, and the large tests make checking every stretch too slow.\n",
  "signature": "def calm_stretch_census(temps: list[int], limit: int) -> int",
  "topic": "monotonic deque",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "category": "stacks-queues",
